            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "deletion",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#*Be aware of any building rules. For instance, the FAA requires you to construct 51% of your plane yourself. Prove this by making a logbook containing photos and videos of your work.<ref>https://www.eaa.org/eaa/aircraft-building/intro-to-aircraft-building/frequently-asked-questions/builders-log</ref>",
                    "#Have your first test flight. Schedule the test with the government agency that certified your plane. The EAA and other flight organizations can help you with this. To pass the test, you have to fly your plane for up to 40 hours total. You can do this within a couple of sessions.<ref>https://www.eaa.org/eaa/aircraft-building/BuilderResources/~/link.aspx?_id=172504857A194AE2AF35AB10C56D03CC&_z=z</ref>[[Image:Build an Airplane Step 16 Version 3.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#*Be aware of any building rules. For instance, the FAA requires you to construct 51% of your plane yourself. Prove this by making a logbook containing photos and videos of your work.<ref>https://www.eaa.org/en/eaa/aviation-communities-and-interests/homebuilt-aircraft-and-homebuilt-aircraft-kits/frequently-asked-questions/builders-log</ref>",
                    "#Have your first test flight. Schedule the test with the government agency that certified your plane. The EAA and other flight organizations can help you with this. To pass the test, you have to fly your plane for up to 40 hours total. You can do this within a couple of sessions.<ref>https://www.eaa.org/en/eaa/aviation-communities-and-interests/homebuilt-aircraft-and-homebuilt-aircraft-kits/how-to-build-an-airplane/answers-to-questions-before-building</ref>[[Image:Build an Airplane Step 16 Version 3.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
